    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24358" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δήμαρχ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, at
		Athens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>chief official of a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆμος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				184S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				50.6
			</span></i>, Lexap.eund.<i><span class="en">
				43.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				21.5
			</span></i>; also at Cos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Cos</u>
				344
			</span></i>,al.; at Chios, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				687
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>C</u>
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> at Naples,
			one of the <i>chief magistrates</i> of the city, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				5.4.7
			</span></i>; at Eretria, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(9).189.24
			</span></i><span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Rome, = Lat. <i>tribunus plebis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.12.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				6.89
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cor.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
